 "Change the antenna position?": "",
 "It is written everywhere it is stored on this Pi (the wall, and the feeders that can be set from here); the ones that cannot are named in the output. The position is never shown on the wall or in a post.": "",
 "Turning it on runs its author's installer: collectd and rrdtool from apt (signed), its files from GitHub, a few minutes. Turning it off puts back what was there before and keeps its history.": "",
 "Move the gain one step?": "",
 "The decoder restarts with the new gain: a few seconds without aircraft. Go one step at a time, and check again after a day.": "",
 "Social sharing": "",
 "Switching it on starts posting the aircraft worth it to Bluesky, as set in the terminal (radius, rules, gap). Off stops the service; the account stays.": "",
 "Hardware watchdog": "",
 "If the Pi freezes completely, its own chip restarts it after about 10 seconds. Off takes the setting away again.": "",
 "Update ZenithBoard and the wall?": "",
 "Seconds. The wall restarts, so this page reconnects by itself. The feeders are left as they are.": "",
 "Update everything?": "",
 "ZenithBoard, the decoder and every feeder, one after the other: several minutes. The wall restarts during it; this page follows. A new GitHub signing key is never accepted from here: the update says so, and it is answered over SSH.": "",
 "Sign computers in with a phone": "",
 "When on, a computer's sign-in page shows a QR code. A phone already signed in scans it, sees the computer, its address and a four-digit code, and says yes: the computer is signed in, no password. Off again: computers use the password.": "",
 "Delete the console's backup?": "",
 "Only the copy kept here for download: the files you already downloaded, and the Pi itself, are not touched.": "",
 "Tailscale": "",
 "Switching it on installs Tailscale the first time (from its own repository, a few minutes), then prints a sign-in link in this card: open it, sign in to YOUR Tailscale account, approve the Pi. The wall then answers your Tailscale devices too. Off disconnects the Pi from your Tailscale network; it stays installed. The wall restarts either way: this page reconnects by itself.": "",
 "The console over Tailscale": "",
 "On: the devices signed in to your Tailscale account can open this console too (encrypted by Tailscale; the password still applies). Off: your home network only. The wall restarts: this page reconnects by itself.": "",
 "Turn the console off?": "",
 "Its pages stop answering at once, this one included. Turn it on again over SSH: sudo zenithboard console on": "",
