 "Putting a backup back (the import)": "",
 "In the terminal of the Pi that receives it: sudo zenithboard backup restore FILE (or the menu: 6 Backup → 2 Put a backup back). It shows what the file holds, asks you to type RESTORE, and keeps what it replaces.": "",
 "Not from this page, on purpose: a restore replaces data and runs installers as root, like the other steps that ask for a typed word.": "",
 "This copy leaves the networks' identities out (keys never travel through this page). To move to a new card, make the full one in the terminal: sudo zenithboard backup make.": "",
